# The id -> word map of the layout before CONFIG_LAYOUT_VERSION_MAGIC existed: 17 bands plus
# general coverage (18 slots per band block), the filter path memories at 329 and
# EEPROM_FIRST_UNUSED 432. UiConfiguration_OldLayoutAddress() in ui_configuration.c translates
# a current id into this layout, and make config-upgrade-check compiles that function and
# compares it with this file and the record of the current marker.
#
# Taken from the header and the ConfigEntry table of 7b79ec8f (the commit that renumbered the
# bands and introduced the marker): every numeric EEPROM_ define of that header, both words of
# every ConfigEntry_Int32 row under the row name, and the two blocks that only have a base
# define - the six per band memories and the 25 filter path memories.
#
#
# The band plan of that layout, in slot order. The map names the per band words by position, so
# without this line the translation check could only compare a band block with its own range and a
# branch that trades two bands would pass. The last slot is general coverage, which had a memory
# there but is not a selectable band in the current layout.
#bands BAND_MODE_80 BAND_MODE_60 BAND_MODE_40 BAND_MODE_30 BAND_MODE_20 BAND_MODE_17 BAND_MODE_15 BAND_MODE_12 BAND_MODE_10 BAND_MODE_6 BAND_MODE_4 BAND_MODE_2 BAND_MODE_70 BAND_MODE_23 BAND_MODE_2200 BAND_MODE_630 BAND_MODE_160 BAND_MODE_GEN
#
# One "word owner" line per claimed word. This file is history, not generated: nothing rewrites
# it, and a word of it moving means the address translation is compared with the wrong layout.
